Subject: [PATCH] fritchii-pr700 v2, incremental on T82 (0451 applied): takes 0451's InvalidationAccumulator hunks

fritchii-pr700 v2, incremental on T82 (0451 applied): takes 0451's InvalidationAccumulator hunks
back, as Fritchii v5.1 did. The result is the same tree as replacing 0451 with
fritchii-pr700-v2.diff. EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_PR700=1 keeps only the QueryCacheBase::IterateCache early
exit (query_cache_base.h is not touched here).

Upstream: zortos293/Lichii#700 (zortos293), ported to Fritchii in f9c0e2d611 (Frizti,
fritchii-v5); its accumulator half rolled back by Frizti (with Claude Opus 5.5) in c2d2f50d15
"Revert the accumulator half of the zortos293/Lichii#700 port for Fritchii v5.1" (fritchii-v5.1,
2026-11-09; unchanged in fritchii-v5.2).

Why: rounding a write's invalidation out to whole 32-byte blocks reaches bytes the CPU did not
write; when those are GPU-written and not yet in guest memory, the invalidation reloads stale guest
bytes over them (Fritchii's owner: glowing geometry over the Hyrule Field drawbridge, the Kakariko
graveyard stale-vertex class). Here MemoryManager::FlushCaching -> RasterizerVulkan::
InnerInvalidation -> BufferCache::WriteMemory drops the GPU-modified state of exactly the range it
is given, so the same applies. invalidation_accumulator.h goes back to the base commit's bytes
(its old arithmetic was what T82 ran with the switch unset).

diff --git a/src/video_core/invalidation_accumulator.h b/src/video_core/invalidation_accumulator.h
index 40f5cfa..eb18856 100644
--- a/src/video_core/invalidation_accumulator.h
+++ b/src/video_core/invalidation_accumulator.h
@@ -10,7 +10,6 @@
 #include <vector>
 
 #include "common/common_types.h"
-#include "common/pe_switch.h"
 
 namespace VideoCommon {
 
@@ -22,14 +21,8 @@ public:
     void Add(GPUVAddr address, size_t size) noexcept {
         auto const end_address = start_address + accumulated_size;
         if (!(address >= start_address && address + size <= end_address)) {
-            // EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_PR700=1 (zortos293/Lichii#700, Fritchii f9c0e2d611): the range runs
-            // from the start of the first 32-byte block the write touches to the end of the last
-            // one. Unset, the size is taken before the address is aligned down, so a write past its
-            // block's start gets a range ending short of it (a lone word at 0x54 gives [0x40, 0x4c)).
-            const GPUVAddr first_block = address & atomicity_mask;
-            size = ((address + size + atomicity_size_mask) & atomicity_mask) -
-                   (BlockFix() ? first_block : address);
-            address = first_block;
+            size = ((address + size + atomicity_size_mask) & atomicity_mask) - address;
+            address = address & atomicity_mask;
             if (start_address == 0) {
                 start_address = address;
                 accumulated_size = size;
@@ -59,11 +52,6 @@ public:
     }
 
 private:
-    static bool BlockFix() noexcept {
-        static const bool on = ::Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_PR700");
-        return on;
-    }
-
     static constexpr size_t atomicity_bits = 5;
     static constexpr size_t atomicity_size = 1ULL << atomicity_bits;
     static constexpr size_t atomicity_size_mask = atomicity_size - 1;
